--- !u!114 &1356921811
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1356921809}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Was it a good idea to embark on a 20-mile backpacking trip when I couldn't
    run a mile without stopping? The question seemed to answer itself. I had gone
    from sea level to an eleven-thousand-foot elevation within a day and my lungs
    let me know of it. With chapped lips, bruised arms, and a sunburned face I stood
    out like a sore thumb in the crowd of experienced hikers. Every painful step
    or sharp inhale asked the same question.  Why, I implored myself, did you say
    yes to something you were so underqualified for? \n\nI did not know the answer
    myself. As the throbbing feet faded into the background of my thoughts, I questioned
    why humans do anything at all. What is the purpose of art? Does everything need
    to have a meaning? By the second day, I had fallen into a rhythm. Colorado's
    white-capped peaks loomed in the distance and wildflowers bloomed in the valley
    below. My pain, while present, was now a part of the grand experience. Philosophical
    thought that was difficult to comprehend at home seemed to come naturally now.
    Somewhere between stepping over pinecones and wading through creeks, it clicked.
    Did there need to be a reason to do anything? There was something beautiful about
    trekking an obscene amount of miles for no reason. Something inherently human
    about stretching your body to its physical limits."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f0dbf9beddd0aba4fb565d16dd73ee29, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -5161710039739289296, guid: f0dbf9beddd0aba4fb565d16dd73ee29, type: 2}
